WEBVTT

00:01.200 --> 00:04.770
Amir Gaul is everything to me.

00:04.770 --> 00:06.800
He's my life.

00:06.800 --> 00:11.600
Amir Gaul is the one I love.

00:12.510 --> 00:15.140
You care about him that much?

00:16.410 --> 00:19.210
You want him that much?!

00:20.880 --> 00:23.080
Then, I'll give him to you.

00:23.080 --> 00:24.880
You can have him!

00:28.520 --> 00:30.990
My Amir Gaul...

00:44.640 --> 00:52.250
Far away from the town where I was born

00:52.250 --> 00:55.420
I am singing

00:55.420 --> 01:03.060
Tucking my weak heart and my wavering feelings

01:03.060 --> 01:06.330
Away in my pocket

01:06.330 --> 01:11.870
Toward where I hear someone calling me

01:11.870 --> 01:16.910
Toward the unknown road

01:16.910 --> 01:22.340
I'll walk

01:22.340 --> 01:27.750
I'll move forward

01:27.750 --> 01:32.590
Not for someone else's sake

01:32.590 --> 01:38.060
But just as I am, so that I can take pride

01:38.060 --> 01:43.530
Just as the sun rises at dawn

01:43.530 --> 01:48.770
I pick out a melody with my voice

01:48.770 --> 01:52.800
Ephemerally yet strongly

01:54.440 --> 01:57.970
I live

02:03.950 --> 02:07.650
Episode 45
The Girl Confined to the Castle

02:09.960 --> 02:11.930
That's Tusk's ...

02:12.660 --> 02:16.620
Boy, hand over Amir Gaul.

02:17.200 --> 02:19.400
He belongs to Tusk.

02:19.400 --> 02:20.670
No!

02:20.670 --> 02:22.940
Amir Gaul belongs to me!

02:22.940 --> 02:24.740
I won't let anyone else have him.

02:24.740 --> 02:27.110
Now, Zed, give him to me.

02:27.110 --> 02:29.410
Give Amir Gaul to me!

02:32.010 --> 02:33.640
Mom!

02:34.180 --> 02:36.520
Stay there and keep quiet.

02:36.520 --> 02:39.690
Now, how about you hand over Amir Gaul?

02:39.690 --> 02:41.310
Garyu!

02:45.290 --> 02:46.920
Rambos!

02:52.800 --> 02:55.430
I'll be taking those key spirits back.

02:57.210 --> 02:59.000
Why, you...

03:01.010 --> 03:02.810
Out of the way!

03:04.680 --> 03:06.310
Zed...

03:06.880 --> 03:08.510
Apcarel!

03:13.050 --> 03:14.680
Mom!

03:25.930 --> 03:27.730
Oh, damn!

03:33.110 --> 03:34.310
Apcarel?

03:34.310 --> 03:35.810
Damn it...

03:35.810 --> 03:37.610
Amir Gaul!

03:45.220 --> 03:48.060
So, here you are, Amir Gaul.

03:48.060 --> 03:50.680
Get him, key spirits.

04:16.650 --> 04:19.350
Not going to go so easily, eh?

04:19.350 --> 04:22.320
That's the strongest key spirit for you!

04:27.830 --> 04:29.800
What's that?

04:30.770 --> 04:32.200
That's ...

04:32.200 --> 04:34.140
The Seekers!

04:34.140 --> 04:36.040
What are they doing here?

04:36.040 --> 04:39.710
Damn it, they'll be trouble.

04:39.710 --> 04:40.780
There's no help for it.

04:40.780 --> 04:42.480
I'll come back later.

04:42.480 --> 04:44.600
Pronimo! Monadi!

04:46.550 --> 04:49.150
Just you wait, boy.

04:49.150 --> 04:51.250
I will have Amir Gaul, mark my word.

04:51.250 --> 04:53.220
Hold it right there!

05:03.100 --> 05:06.900
Mom, where did you go?

05:09.000 --> 05:15.380
I give you my most heartfelt apologies
for the errors of my emissary.

05:15.380 --> 05:17.480
The past is past.

05:17.480 --> 05:19.480
We will not censure you.

05:19.480 --> 05:26.050
Never mind that, we are quite
interested in the Seekers.

05:26.050 --> 05:29.720
You have been shrouded in
mystery for some time.

05:29.720 --> 05:34.060
I've heard that the Seekers are
a peace-loving race.

05:34.060 --> 05:40.230
Why don't our countries take this
opportunity to form an alliance?

05:40.230 --> 05:43.710
If we can join forces with you,

05:43.710 --> 05:47.840
we can stand against the threat of Tusk.

05:48.540 --> 05:51.810
We take neither side in this.

05:51.810 --> 05:53.850
I cannot do as you ask.

05:53.850 --> 05:55.350
What?!

05:55.350 --> 05:57.650
Our principal objective

05:57.650 --> 06:03.110
is to prevent this world's six key spirits
from being gathered in one place.

06:03.760 --> 06:05.760
In work to that end,

06:05.760 --> 06:08.560
you will have our full and
unhesitating cooperation.

06:11.470 --> 06:13.200
Oh, Lady Sagiri.

06:13.200 --> 06:15.740
Are you feeling all right?

06:15.740 --> 06:18.570
Yeah, I'm okay.

06:18.570 --> 06:21.540
I see, thank goodness.

06:21.540 --> 06:23.670
Let us go home then.

06:24.080 --> 06:25.980
I don't want to go!

06:25.980 --> 06:28.180
I'm going to look for Noah!

06:28.180 --> 06:29.520
Lady Sagiri!

06:29.520 --> 06:33.790
The fate of the Seekers is in your hands!

06:33.790 --> 06:37.750
We will brook no further selfishness.

06:39.360 --> 06:41.330
You understand?

06:41.330 --> 06:42.900
Then, let us go.

06:42.900 --> 06:44.690
Wait a minute.

06:46.200 --> 06:47.540
Zed...

06:47.540 --> 06:50.160
What do you want, Zed?

06:52.170 --> 06:56.480
Would you tell me about my mom?

06:56.480 --> 07:00.350
What's the connection between
her and you people?

07:00.350 --> 07:04.290
So, you're Sara's son Zed?

07:04.290 --> 07:06.410
You know about me too?

07:07.790 --> 07:10.460
You look just like your father.

07:10.460 --> 07:11.830
Dad...

07:11.830 --> 07:14.100
You know Dad, too?!

07:14.100 --> 07:18.570
If you want to hear the story,
come to our ship.

07:18.570 --> 07:22.370
Now, Lady Sagiri, let's go.

07:26.910 --> 07:29.210
My dad...

07:34.380 --> 07:37.450
Weren't you going to get back Amir Gaul?

07:37.450 --> 07:38.450
Eh, Xeem?!

07:38.450 --> 07:42.590
I never imagined the Seekers
were making a move,

07:42.590 --> 07:45.890
but I did not come back empty-handed.

07:46.830 --> 07:48.800
There are three left.

07:48.800 --> 07:51.770
They day when they are all ours is not far off,

07:51.770 --> 07:55.340
and on that day, Mirred will become the savior,

07:55.340 --> 07:57.840
and Tusk will change this world.

07:57.840 --> 07:59.770
Mirred, eh?

07:59.770 --> 08:04.070
Does that girl really have the power to do it?

08:04.680 --> 08:07.820
What are you trying to say, Molima?

08:07.820 --> 08:11.270
Oh, nothing at all.

08:17.690 --> 08:20.430
I'm looking forward to the next time
we can see each other.

08:20.430 --> 08:21.900
Yeah...

08:21.900 --> 08:24.600
Okay, keep your chin up, Sagiri.

08:24.600 --> 08:27.200
You too, Roya.

08:27.200 --> 08:31.010
Of course! I always do!

08:31.010 --> 08:34.110
Let us go, Lady Sagiri.

08:34.110 --> 08:36.410
Go on now, time to go.

08:41.650 --> 08:44.020
See you later, then.

08:44.020 --> 08:47.150
Yeah, take care.

08:52.360 --> 08:57.660
I wonder why I feel like I'll never see Zed again?

09:06.310 --> 09:10.110
I'm sorry, Zed.

09:33.370 --> 09:36.670
It sounds like Gitra's a little irritated today.

09:38.270 --> 09:40.570
What are you looking at?

09:41.710 --> 09:43.610
Oh, Molima.

09:43.610 --> 09:45.750
I was watching the sky.

09:45.750 --> 09:47.650
The sky?

09:47.650 --> 09:50.990
The only part of the outside world I can look at

09:50.990 --> 09:55.020
is the tiny patch of sky you can
see through this window.

09:55.020 --> 09:57.660
Ever since I can remember,

09:57.660 --> 10:01.290
it's been the only scenery I've ever seen.

10:02.830 --> 10:06.730
I'm told the sky is enormously vast.

10:06.730 --> 10:11.640
Someday, I'd like to see that sky
spreading in front of me.

10:11.640 --> 10:14.280
The true, vast sky!

10:14.280 --> 10:16.570
Then, go ahead and see it.

10:22.320 --> 10:25.650
If you're our future savior,

10:25.650 --> 10:29.780
you must know how to use spell shards.

11:09.530 --> 11:11.160
This...

11:12.100 --> 11:14.070
...is the true sky!

11:17.940 --> 11:22.040
The outside world is full of dangers
you've never known.

11:22.040 --> 11:24.680
If you're the true savior,

11:24.680 --> 11:27.480
I trust you'll be able to return alive.

11:36.960 --> 11:39.390
She's sleeping soundly.

11:39.390 --> 11:42.520
She must have been quite tired.

11:45.030 --> 11:46.830
Please tell me...

11:47.330 --> 11:50.960
...about my mom and my dad.

11:53.370 --> 11:57.580
I must begin by telling you of your father.

11:57.580 --> 12:02.210
Your father was one of the Seekers.

12:03.320 --> 12:07.450
Dad was one of the Seekers?

12:09.060 --> 12:12.930
What?! Lady Mirred is gone?!

12:12.930 --> 12:16.430
There's no way she could have
gotten out of there alone.

12:16.430 --> 12:18.400
Who the hell did this?!

12:19.000 --> 12:20.770
Find her at once!

12:20.770 --> 12:22.400
Yes, sir!

12:23.000 --> 12:24.630
What?!

12:36.650 --> 12:38.780
W..Water?

12:46.590 --> 12:50.390
This must be a " lake" !

12:51.600 --> 12:54.200
It's sparkling!

12:54.200 --> 12:56.670
It's just like a jewel!

13:08.680 --> 13:15.660
Your father landed in Calm,
a new territory, to study it.

13:15.660 --> 13:17.120
Calm?

13:17.120 --> 13:18.260
Yes...

13:18.260 --> 13:24.220
To us, Calm was a newly-discovered land.

13:27.540 --> 13:31.910
It was your father's job to investigate things

13:31.910 --> 13:37.540
like whether there were key spirits
or shard casters there.

13:38.710 --> 13:43.250
However, he was attacked by a Tuskan soldier
who infiltrated Calm after him,

13:43.250 --> 13:45.220
and he was gravely injured.

13:45.820 --> 13:51.780
The one who happened to find and save
him was your mother, Sara.

13:53.360 --> 13:55.160
I see...

13:55.600 --> 14:01.470
But injuries from that battle
eventually claimed his life,

14:01.470 --> 14:04.910
leaving Sara and her unborn child behind.

14:04.910 --> 14:06.810
Her unborn child...

14:06.810 --> 14:09.610
Yes, you.

14:11.580 --> 14:16.680
So, Amir Gaul really did choose me,

14:16.680 --> 14:18.810
and not her?

15:17.140 --> 15:20.780
The old man, I mean Zico,

15:20.780 --> 15:25.740
told me my power might be needed
to stop this fighting.

15:26.350 --> 15:28.060
Yes...

15:28.060 --> 15:30.260
According to this world's legend,

15:30.260 --> 15:37.730
the one who assembles all the key spirits
will be granted Tusker's power.

15:37.730 --> 15:42.100
It is said his power could even destroy the world.

15:42.100 --> 15:48.040
Therefore, naturally, that person could
become ruler of this world.

15:48.040 --> 15:51.550
The ruler? Not the savior?

15:51.550 --> 15:54.720
That depends on how they use the power.

15:54.720 --> 15:58.520
Each land has someone they call the " savior, "

15:58.520 --> 16:02.720
but only one person can gain
the power of Tusker.

16:02.720 --> 16:06.160
If Lady Sagiri is that savior,

16:06.160 --> 16:09.330
then the balance of this world
will surely be maintained.

16:09.330 --> 16:14.130
Believing that, I have entrusted everything to her.

16:14.900 --> 16:16.770
To Sagiri...

16:16.770 --> 16:22.280
But it would be better for the key spirits
never to come together at all.

16:22.280 --> 16:25.810
Is the power really that fearsome?

16:25.810 --> 16:27.780
Zed...

16:27.780 --> 16:33.150
Mere humans must not touch a god's power.

16:33.150 --> 16:36.280
That is the law of nature.

16:47.130 --> 16:50.590
It better not have been Gitra.

16:53.910 --> 16:57.210
Where did Lady Mirred go?

17:00.980 --> 17:04.280
She's never been outside before!

17:04.280 --> 17:06.390
If I don't find her fast...

17:06.390 --> 17:08.180
Lady Mirred...

17:12.990 --> 17:15.060
We've finally found her!

17:15.060 --> 17:16.530
It's just like they said!

17:16.530 --> 17:19.830
Behold, the key spirit Dynamis!

17:20.630 --> 17:26.040
Xeem, Gitra, this child will one day be the savior,

17:26.040 --> 17:29.340
and she will be the key to Tusk's prosperity!

17:31.350 --> 17:32.780
In the end,

17:32.780 --> 17:36.910
Father left this world without ever disclosing
where Lady Mirred had been born.

17:38.220 --> 17:42.720
Growing up caged away,
not knowing her parents...

17:42.720 --> 17:45.350
Just think what her days were like!

17:49.260 --> 17:53.220
In the end, nobody thinks about her feelings.

17:56.770 --> 17:59.110
It was my first time...

17:59.110 --> 18:02.980
It's my first time seeing everything, so...

18:02.980 --> 18:04.310
Are you unable to stand?

18:04.310 --> 18:05.940
Oh, no!

18:07.480 --> 18:09.880
What a large creature he was.

18:09.880 --> 18:12.510
I wonder if he lived in this lake?

18:13.390 --> 18:16.360
You don't seem to be from Tusk.

18:17.390 --> 18:21.020
You must have seen many skies!

18:22.230 --> 18:26.860
You see, you have the eyes of someone
who's seen many things.

18:29.000 --> 18:32.810
Is the sky this vast where you were born too?

18:32.810 --> 18:35.740
What color is it?

18:35.740 --> 18:38.780
Have you ever seen the sky at night?

18:38.780 --> 18:43.180
The sun never sets in this land,
so night never comes.

18:43.180 --> 18:45.820
I want to see the night sky too.

18:45.820 --> 18:49.260
They call it a "star-spangled sky," right?

18:49.260 --> 18:51.190
There is something like a starry sky here,

18:51.190 --> 18:53.990
even if it's not the real thing.

18:55.430 --> 18:57.870
Please, take me there!

18:57.870 --> 19:00.130
I want to see all kinds of things!

19:00.130 --> 19:02.760
Lots of things, while I still can!

19:15.780 --> 19:19.080
Sagiri, a savior...

19:20.750 --> 19:23.360
Zed, look for Noah!

19:23.360 --> 19:25.150
Look for him with me!

19:28.760 --> 19:30.630
Noah...

19:30.630 --> 19:33.260
People called you " savior" too, huh?

19:34.540 --> 19:37.500
Do you want Tusker's power?

19:38.710 --> 19:42.330
Will you come to steal Amir Gaul from me?

19:58.490 --> 20:01.950
Um, it's pitch-dark in here,
and I can't see where I'm ...

20:02.700 --> 20:06.150
It's very slippery right here!

20:08.400 --> 20:12.360
Um, I truly can't see anything...

20:13.110 --> 20:14.510
I'm sorry!

20:14.510 --> 20:16.480
Look in front of you.

20:37.100 --> 20:39.070
So, this is a starry sky!

20:40.070 --> 20:42.970
This is the Cave of Toste.

20:42.970 --> 20:45.510
It just looks like a starry sky
because of a natural phenomenon.

20:45.510 --> 20:47.540
That's all right!

20:47.540 --> 20:50.340
To me, it's still my first starry sky!

20:51.350 --> 20:53.140
Don't move!

20:54.750 --> 20:56.620
Who the hell are you?

20:56.620 --> 20:58.990
What do you want with Lady Mirred?

20:58.990 --> 21:00.920
Gitra, is that your voice I hear?

21:00.920 --> 21:02.860
So, you really are Lady Mirred.

21:02.860 --> 21:04.090
What?!

21:04.090 --> 21:07.060
I was planning to escort her
to the castle after this.

21:07.690 --> 21:09.160
Perfect timing.

21:09.160 --> 21:10.960
I'll leave her to you.

21:12.200 --> 21:15.330
Wait! Who are you?!

21:15.970 --> 21:17.940
My name is Dolga.

21:17.940 --> 21:19.910
You'll find out the rest soon enough.

21:21.240 --> 21:22.870
Dolga...

21:25.310 --> 21:27.110
Master Dolga...

21:37.320 --> 21:39.450
Did you sleep well?

21:40.830 --> 21:44.770
I jumped into this world of my own free will,

21:44.770 --> 21:49.270
but at the same time, it was also because
Amir Gaul was beckoning me.

21:49.270 --> 21:52.400
I don't care whether I'm the savior or not.

21:53.310 --> 21:59.440
If the key spirits are causing the wars,
then I'll stop those wars.

22:02.820 --> 22:06.450
I'm going to Tusk.

22:10.860 --> 22:14.490
Lady Mirred still hasn't been found,

22:14.490 --> 22:17.960
but I've brought a man I'd like
to introduce to you all.

22:17.960 --> 22:19.100
A man?

22:19.100 --> 22:24.230
He will be working with us for the sake of Tusk.

22:30.140 --> 22:32.270
This is Lord Dolga.

22:39.620 --> 22:42.020
I just wanted to get away

22:42.020 --> 22:44.920
From that troublesome place

22:45.860 --> 22:49.230
And flap my wings

22:49.230 --> 22:54.430
How many times have I scolded myself

22:54.430 --> 23:00.070
For still being so immature?

23:01.140 --> 23:05.980
I'll just move with all I've got

23:05.980 --> 23:11.620
Towards that promised place

23:11.620 --> 23:17.220
Ours are true wings

23:17.220 --> 23:24.000
Of very, very beautiful feathers

23:24.000 --> 23:26.700
So we won't succumb

23:26.700 --> 23:33.740
To even the greatest, most intense gust of wind

23:33.740 --> 23:43.820
We must fly far, far away with all we've got

23:43.820 --> 23:49.560
See, now we're one with the wind

23:49.560 --> 23:54.630
And we can look back and laugh at those days

23:54.630 --> 23:57.930
We choked back so many tears

23:59.930 --> 24:03.890
All the way to the ends of the world

24:17.750 --> 24:20.950
Next Time
To the Land Where the Decision Will Be made

24:18.150 --> 24:20.950


Next time,
"To the Land Where the Decision Will Be Made"
